<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 21 September, from 454 to 1981.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">International Day of Peace</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Established by the United Nations in 1981 and observed with a global ceasefire since 2001, the International Day of Peace invites all nations and peoples to commit to peace above all differences and to contribute to building a culture of peace.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/454">454 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,572 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Valentinian III murders his general Aetius</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-iii">Valentinian III</a> killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Flavius Aetius</a> with his own hands during a meeting in Ravenna. The West lost the commander who had checked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>; Valentinian was himself assassinated six months later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1217">1217 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">809 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Sword Brethren defeat Lembitu's Estonians near Viljandi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viljandi">Viljandi</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a> and their Liv and Latgalian allies defeated an Estonian army of 6,000 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lembitu">Lembitu</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sagala">Sakala</a>. Lembitu was killed, as was the crusaders' Liv ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caupo">Caupo of Turaida</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-st-matthews-day">Battle of St Matthew's Day</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lembitu">Lembitu</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caupo">Caupo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1327">1327 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">699 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Deposed Edward II dies at Berkeley Castle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edward II was announced dead at Berkeley Castle, almost certainly murdered on the orders of Queen Isabella and Roger Mortimer. The later tale of a red-hot poker is unsupported.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1435">1435 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">591 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Arras reconciles France and Burgundy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a>, duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, recognised Charles VII as king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in return for the towns of the Somme, ending Burgundy's alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> fell to Charles the next year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-arras-1435">Treaty of Arras (1435)</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1745">1745 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">281 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jacobites rout a government army at Prestonpans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-edward-stuart">Bonnie Prince Charlie</a>'s Highlanders routed Sir John Cope's army in a few minutes near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>. The victory encouraged the Jacobite invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, which turned back at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derby">Derby</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fire destroys up to 1,000 buildings in occupied New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Breaking out in the early days of the British occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> City, the Great Fire burned through the night of 20 September into the morning of the 21st and destroyed up to 1,000 buildings.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1792">1792 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The National Convention abolishes the French monarchy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On its first full day, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">National Convention</a>, created after the insurrection of 10 August 1792, proclaimed the abolition of the French monarchy, giving rise to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-first-republic">French First Republic</a>. In 1793 it tried and executed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">National Convention</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1866">1866 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">160 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">H. G. Wells is born in Bromley</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Herbert George <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">Wells</a> was born in Kent to a shopkeeper's family. His novels The Time Machine and The War of the Worlds helped found modern science fiction.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1981">1981 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">45 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Belize becomes independent</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former British Honduras became independent as Belize, with George Price as prime minister. British troops remained because <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a> claimed the territory; it recognised Belize in 1991.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 21 September <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-elector-of-brandenburg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-elector-of-brandenburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick I, Elector of Brandenburg</span><span class="tp">1371–1440</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-iii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick III, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1415–1493</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/girolamo-savonarola"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/girolamo-savonarola.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Girolamo Savonarola</span><span class="tp">1452–1498</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hedwig-jagiellon-duchess-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hedwig-jagiellon-duchess-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hedwig Jagiellon, Duchess of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1457–1502</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-jolliet"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-jolliet.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis Jolliet</span><span class="tp">1645–1700</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louise-marie-therese-of-artois"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louise-marie-therese-of-artois.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louise Marie Thérèse of Artois</span><span class="tp">1819–1864</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francesc-macia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francesc-macia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francesc Macià</span><span class="tp">1859–1933</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kevin-rudd"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kevin-rudd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kevin Rudd</span><span class="tp">b. 1957</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 21 September <span class="n">10</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/virgil"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/virgil.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Virgil</span><span class="tp">70–19 BCE</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/flavius-aetius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Flavius Aetius</span><span class="tp">c. 391–454</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/otto-william-count-of-burgundy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/otto-william-count-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Otto-William, Count of Burgundy</span><span class="tp">c. 958–1026</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lembitu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lembitu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lembitu</span><span class="tp">d. 1217</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-ii-of-england"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-ii-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward II of England</span><span class="tp">1284–1327</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ivan-mazepa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ivan-mazepa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ivan Mazepa</span><span class="tp">1639–1709</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jai-singh-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jai-singh-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jai Singh II</span><span class="tp">1688–1743</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/chief-joseph"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Chief Joseph</span><span class="tp">1840–1904</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/haakon-vii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/haakon-vii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Haakon VII</span><span class="tp">1872–1957</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bernardo-houssay"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bernardo-houssay.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bernardo Houssay</span><span class="tp">1887–1971</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
